---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { contact, hrefs } from "../config/site";

/* ============================================================
   JVG SHIPPING PROCESS — FAIR PLAY GUARANTEE variant.
   noIndex hand-out link (see jvg-shipping-process.astro notes).
   Differences from the base page: payment is sent after the
   same-day arrival inspection (not at the FedEx counter), there
   is a 6th step, and the Fair-Play Guarantee section spells out
   the renegotiate-or-return terms. Keep the FedEx account number
   and Fraser Drive shipping address EXACTLY as on live.

   Copy is deliberately short: sellers read this on a phone, often
   standing in a FedEx parking lot. Every fact from the longer
   original is still here (private Heritage policy, why loose cases
   cause damage, the no-official-center fallback, the full return
   package), just in fewer words. Don't pad it back out.
   ============================================================ */

const SHIP_TO = "47 North Fraser Drive East, Mesa, AZ 85203";
const FEDEX_ACCT = "541950800";
---

<Layout
  title="JVG Shipping Process - Fair Play Guarantee"
  description="Step-by-step instructions for shipping your guitar to Joe's Vintage Guitars, backed by the Fair-Play Guarantee: free insured shipping, same-day inspection, and same-day payment."
  canonical="/jvg-shipping-process-2/"
  noIndex={true}
>
  <section class="ship-title-bar">
    <div class="ship-inner"><h1>JVG Shipping Process</h1><p class="ship-sub">Backed by the Fair-Play Guarantee</p></div>
  </section>

  <section class="ship-body">
    <div class="ship-inner">
      <p class="ship-lede">
        Shipping me your guitar from out of state is simple, secure, and backed by a fair-play
        guarantee. Here is exactly how it works, start to finish.
      </p>

      <div class="ship-reviews">
        <p class="ship-reviews__lead">Hundreds of sellers have already done this.</p>
        <p>Click below to read reviews from people who sold me a guitar using this same process.</p>
        <a
          class="ship-reviews__btn"
          href={hrefs.googleReviews}
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
        >
          Read Reviews From People Who Sold Me Their Guitar
        </a>
      </div>

      <h2>The Process at a Glance</h2>
      <p>Six steps. Your part is done once the guitar is at FedEx; everything after that is on me.</p>
      <div class="ship-callout">
        <ul>
          <li><strong>You pay nothing.</strong> All packing and shipping costs are mine.</li>
          <li><strong>Fully insured</strong> in transit under our private Heritage Musical Instrument policy, which is better coverage than FedEx offers.</li>
          <li><strong>Same-day inspection and payment.</strong> Your guitar is inspected the day it arrives and payment is sent immediately after.</li>
          <li><strong>Fair-Play Guarantee.</strong> If the guitar’s originality or condition differs from what we discussed, we renegotiate fairly, or I ship it back at my cost with a free professional setup, free photographs, and a signed authentication letter.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <h2><span class="ship-step">Step 1</span> Send Me Your Info</h2>
      <p>
        Text or email me a photo of your driver’s license along with your preferred email address. The
        license photo is strictly for fraud prevention; it confirms the sale on both sides and protects
        us both. Your information stays private and is never shared.
      </p>

      <h2><span class="ship-step">Step 2</span> Pack the Inside of the Case</h2>
      <p>
        This is the most important thing you’ll do. Fill every empty space in the case so the guitar
        can’t move at all. Newspaper, old t-shirts, towels, paper towels, and foam all work. Then close
        the case and shake it hard in every direction. Hear or feel anything shift? Add more padding.
      </p>
      <div class="ship-warn">
        <strong>No bubble wrap inside the case.</strong> It can react with the nitrocellulose lacquer on
        vintage finishes and leave permanent marks or stick to the finish over time. Soft cloth,
        newspaper, and paper towels are all safe. Bubble wrap outside the case is fine, just never
        touching the guitar.
      </div>
      <p class="ship-note">
        Why it matters: a loose guitar inside its case is the number one cause of shipping damage. Even
        with perfect outer packing, a guitar rattling around inside its own case can crack a headstock
        or dent the body. Two minutes of stuffing t-shirts around the neck and body prevents almost
        every shipping problem I’ve seen.
      </p>

      <h2><span class="ship-step">Step 3</span> Take It to FedEx</h2>
      <div class="ship-exact">
        <p class="ship-exact__label">It has to be this, word for word:</p>
        <p class="ship-exact__name">FedEx Office Print &amp; Ship Center</p>
        <p class="ship-exact__note">
          If the sign on the building says anything else, it is the wrong place. A
          “FedEx Authorized ShipCenter,” a plain “FedEx Ship Center,” or any pack-and-ship store with
          a FedEx sign in the window is a different business and cannot do this. Not sure? Text me the
          name before you hand over the guitar.
        </p>
      </div>
      <p>
        Only the real locations have the staff, the materials, and the guitar-sized boxes I need them
        to use. Call ahead to confirm they have a guitar box in stock; most do, and the call saves you
        a wasted trip. Phone tip: when the automated menu picks up, press 7 to go straight through to a
        person at that location.
      </p>
      <p>
        No FedEx Office Print &amp; Ship Center near you? Tell me before you head out and I’ll arrange
        a pickup or an alternative.
      </p>

      <h2><span class="ship-step">Step 4</span> At the Counter</h2>
      <p>
        Text me a photo of the guitar on the counter; that’s my signal everything is on track. Then hand
        it to a FedEx employee, ask them to pack it very tightly so nothing moves inside the box when
        shaken, and give them this:
      </p>
      <table class="ship-table">
        <tbody>
          <tr><th>FedEx Account #</th><td>{FEDEX_ACCT}</td></tr>
          <tr><th>Charge to Account</th><td>Packaging + Shipping (you won’t pay a cent)</td></tr>
          <tr><th>Ship To</th><td>{SHIP_TO}</td></tr>
          <tr><th>Return Address</th><td>Your own address</td></tr>
          <tr><th>Shipping Speed</th><td>Cheapest option, unless I’ve told you otherwise</td></tr>
          <tr><th>Insurance</th><td>None. See the note below.</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
      <p class="ship-note">
        We decline FedEx’s insurance on purpose. Every guitar we buy is covered under our private
        Heritage Musical Instrument policy, which offers broader coverage and a far smoother claims
        process. Your guitar is insured from the moment it leaves your hands until it reaches my shop.
      </p>

      <h2><span class="ship-step">Step 5</span> Scan, Drop Off, and You’re Done</h2>
      <p>
        Once it’s packed and labeled, have the FedEx employee scan the label and hand you the drop-off
        receipt. Text me a photo of that receipt and your part is finished. The guitar is now insured,
        tracked, and on its way. Follow the tracking number, or just wait for my text when it lands.
      </p>

      <h2><span class="ship-step">Step 6</span> Arrival, Inspection, Payment</h2>
      <p>
        I inspect your guitar the same day it arrives. No sitting around for a week waiting on a dealer
        to get to it. If it matches what we discussed, payment goes out that same day by your preferred
        method. Most sellers have the money in their account within hours of the guitar reaching my shop.
      </p>

      <h2>Our Fair-Play Guarantee</h2>
      <p>
        Vintage guitars have long histories. A pickup was swapped decades ago, a tuner was replaced, a
        finish was touched up, and sometimes even the current owner has no idea. If what I find differs
        from what we discussed, I call you that same day, walk you through it, explain how it affects
        value, and propose a fair revised price. From there it’s your call:
      </p>
      <div class="ship-callout">
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Accept the new price.</strong> Payment goes out the same day. No hassle, no delays.</li>
          <li><strong>Take the guitar back.</strong> I ship it home at my cost, fully insured, with everything below included.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <p>Send it back and it returns to you with:</p>
      <ul class="ship-check">
        <li>A free professional setup: intonation, action, and neck relief dialed in by a working luthier.</li>
        <li>A set of free professional photographs, for insurance, a future sale, or your own records.</li>
        <li>A free written and signed authentication letter covering the guitar’s originality, modifications, and historical context. That letter normally costs hundreds of dollars from an outside appraiser.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        You lose nothing. Most sellers who go this route end up with a better playing, better documented
        guitar than the one they sent, at zero cost.
      </p>

      <h2>Payment Options</h2>
      <p>
        Use whatever you already trust: PayPal, Venmo, Zelle, Cash App, wire transfer, or a mailed check.
      </p>
      <p class="ship-note">
        One note on limits: Venmo, Zelle, Cash App, and PayPal all cap how much you can receive per day
        or per transfer. On a higher-dollar sale, tell me your preferred method in advance so we can
        confirm it’ll clear in one shot, or plan a quick wire transfer instead.
      </p>

      <h2>Quick Reference Checklist</h2>
      <ul class="ship-check">
        <li>Email address and driver’s license photo sent</li>
        <li>Case packed tight with soft materials only, no bubble wrap</li>
        <li>Called ahead about a guitar box (press 7 if you get the robot)</li>
        <li>Sign checked: it reads FedEx Office Print &amp; Ship Center, word for word</li>
        <li>Photo of the guitar on the counter texted to me</li>
        <li>FedEx account #{FEDEX_ACCT} and the Mesa, AZ address given</li>
        <li>Cheapest shipping selected, unless I specified otherwise</li>
        <li>FedEx insurance declined</li>
        <li>Drop-off receipt photo texted to me</li>
        <li>Payment method confirmed in advance</li>
      </ul>

      <p class="ship-reviews__inline">
        Still deciding? <a href={hrefs.googleReviews} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Read the
        reviews from sellers who shipped their guitars exactly this way</a>.
      </p>

      <div class="ship-contact">
        <p><strong>Questions? Text me anytime.</strong></p>
        <p>
          If anything is unclear before, during, or after your trip to FedEx, reach out. I’d rather
          answer ten questions than have you guess at any of it.
        </p>
        <p>
          Phone/Text: <a href={hrefs.tel}>{contact.phone}</a><br />
          Email: <a href={hrefs.mailto}>{contact.email}</a><br />
          Shipping Address: {SHIP_TO}<br />
          FedEx Account #: {FEDEX_ACCT}
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .ship-inner { max-width: 820px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 0 24px; }
  .ship-title-bar {
    background: var(--color-brand-rust-dark, #682412);
    padding: 180px 24px 48px;
    text-align: center;
  }
  .ship-title-bar h1 {
    margin: 0;
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: clamp(32px, 5vw, 54px);
    color: var(--color-brand-cream);
    line-height: 1.1;
  }
  .ship-sub {
    margin: 10px 0 0;
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: clamp(16px, 2.2vw, 22px);
    color: var(--color-brand-brown-tan);
  }
  .ship-body { background: #fff; padding: 44px 0 72px; }
  .ship-body p, .ship-body li {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: 16px;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: var(--color-brand-charcoal);
  }
  .ship-body p { margin: 0 0 16px; }
  .ship-lede { font-size: 18px !important; }
  .ship-note { font-style: italic; }
  .ship-body a { color: var(--color-brand-rust); text-decoration: underline; font-weight: 600; }
  .ship-body h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: 24px;
    color: var(--color-brand-rust-dark);
    margin: 36px 0 12px;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 12px;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
  }
  .ship-step {
    display: inline-block;
    background: var(--color-brand-rust-bright, #be4b25);
    color: #fff;
    font-size: 14px;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    padding: 4px 12px;
    border-radius: 4px;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }
  /* Reviews CTA. Dark rust so it reads as the one clickable thing up top and
     doesn't blend into the cream callouts used elsewhere on the page. */
  .ship-reviews {
    background: var(--color-brand-rust-dark, #682412);
    border-radius: 6px;
    padding: 22px 24px;
    margin: 0 0 20px;
    text-align: center;
  }
  .ship-body .ship-reviews p {
    color: var(--color-brand-cream, #eedfc0);
    margin: 0 0 6px;
  }
  .ship-reviews__lead {
    font-family: var(--font-display) !important;
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: 20px !important;
    letter-spacing: 0.01em;
  }
  .ship-body .ship-reviews__btn {
    display: inline-block;
    margin-top: 12px;
    background: var(--color-brand-cream, #eedfc0);
    color: var(--color-brand-rust-dark, #682412);
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: 15px;
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    text-decoration: none;
    padding: 13px 24px;
    border-radius: 4px;
    line-height: 1.3;
  }
  .ship-body .ship-reviews__btn:hover,
  .ship-body .ship-reviews__btn:focus-visible {
    background: #fff;
    text-decoration: underline;
  }
  .ship-reviews__inline {
    background: var(--color-brand-cream-light, #f9f1de);
    border-left: 4px solid var(--color-brand-rust-bright);
    padding: 14px 18px;
    margin: 24px 0 0 !important;
  }
  .ship-callout {
    background: var(--color-brand-cream-light, #f9f1de);
    border-left: 4px solid var(--color-brand-rust-bright);
    padding: 16px 20px;
    margin: 0 0 16px;
  }
  .ship-callout ul { margin: 0; padding-left: 20px; }
  .ship-callout li { margin-bottom: 6px; }
  .ship-warn {
    background: #f6e0da;
    border-left: 4px solid #842012;
    padding: 14px 18px;
    margin: 0 0 16px;
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: 15px;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: #5a1a0d;
  }
  /* Exact-name callout. The store name is the single easiest thing for a seller
     to get wrong, so it gets its own block with the name set large and literal.
     Do NOT shorten it to "FedEx Print & Ship Center" — the word "Office" is what
     separates the real store from a FedEx Authorized ShipCenter. */
  .ship-exact {
    background: #f6e0da;
    border: 2px solid #842012;
    border-radius: 6px;
    padding: 18px 20px;
    margin: 0 0 16px;
    text-align: center;
  }
  .ship-body .ship-exact p { color: #5a1a0d; margin: 0; }
  .ship-body .ship-exact__label {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: 15px;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }
  /* p.<class> so the name beats the `.ship-body .ship-exact p` colour above it. */
  .ship-body .ship-exact p.ship-exact__name {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: clamp(21px, 3.4vw, 30px);
    line-height: 1.2;
    color: #842012;
    margin: 8px 0 10px;
  }
  .ship-body .ship-exact__note {
    font-size: 15px;
    line-height: 1.6;
    text-align: left;
  }
  .ship-table {
    width: 100%;
    border-collapse: collapse;
    margin: 0 0 18px;
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: 15px;
  }
  .ship-table th, .ship-table td {
    text-align: left;
    padding: 11px 14px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(62, 42, 20, 0.12);
    color: var(--color-brand-charcoal);
    vertical-align: top;
  }
  .ship-table th {
    width: 36%;
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--color-brand-rust-dark);
    white-space: nowrap;
  }
  .ship-check { list-style: none; margin: 0 0 18px; padding: 0; }
  .ship-check li {
    position: relative;
    padding-left: 30px;
    margin-bottom: 9px;
  }
  .ship-check li::before {
    content: "✓";
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    top: 0;
    color: var(--color-brand-rust-bright);
    font-weight: 700;
  }
  .ship-contact {
    margin-top: 36px;
    background: var(--color-brand-cream, #eedfc0);
    padding: 20px 24px;
    border-radius: 6px;
  }
  .ship-contact p { margin: 0 0 8px; }
  @media (max-width: 700px) {
    .ship-title-bar { padding: 120px 16px 36px; }
    .ship-table th { white-space: normal; width: 40%; }
    .ship-reviews { padding: 20px 16px; }
    .ship-body .ship-reviews__btn { font-size: 14px; padding: 12px 18px; }
  }
</style>
